Usage: loki-transform.py convert [OPTIONS]

  Batch-processing mode for Fortran-to-Fortran transformations that employs a
  :class:`Scheduler` to process large numbers of source files.

  Based on the given "mode" string, configuration file, source file paths and
  build arguments the :any:`Scheduler` will perform automatic call-tree
  exploration and apply a set of :any:`Transformation` objects to this call
  tree.

Options:
  -m, --mode TEXT                 Transformation mode, selecting which code
                                  transformations to apply.
  --config PATH                   Path to custom scheduler configuration file
  -b, --build, --out-path PATH    Path to build directory for source
                                  generation.
  -s, --source, --path PATH       Path to search during source exploration.
  -h, --header PATH               Path for additional header file(s).
  --cpp / --no-cpp                Trigger C-preprocessing of source files.
  -I, --include PATH              Path for additional header file(s)
  -D, --define TEXT               Additional symbol definitions for the
                                  C-preprocessor
  --omni-include PATH             Additional path for header files,
                                  specifically for OMNI
  -M, --xmod PATH                 Path for additional .xmod file(s) for OMNI
  --frontend [fp|ofp|omni]        Frontend parser to use (default FP)
  --plan-file PATH                Process pipeline in planning mode and
                                  generate CMake "plan" file.
  -g, --callgraph PATH            Generate and display the subroutine
                                  callgraph.
  --root PATH                     Root path to which all paths are relative
                                  to.
  -l, --log-level [debug|detail|perf|info|warning|error]
                                  Log level to output during batch processing
  --help                          Show this message and exit.
